# Production environment variables.
#
# The core product needs NONE of these to run locally: `npm run dev` boots an
# embedded Postgres and hits the public openFDA and RxNorm APIs with no key.

# Hosted Postgres for production. Neon, Vercel Postgres, Supabase or any
# Postgres 14+ works; the connection string is the only required value.
DATABASE_URL=

# Optional. Set to 1 ONLY to rehearse a production build against the embedded
# database on a laptop. Never set this on a real deployment: /api/health will
# report the embedded driver so a misconfigured deploy is obvious.
# HANDOVER_ALLOW_EMBEDDED=

# Optional. Where the embedded database writes when running locally.
# PGLITE_DATA_DIR=.data/pglite

# Optional. Canonical origin for metadata, OG tags and the MCP manifest.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-deployment.vercel.app